From 17e44c272bae16fd5ff0ca61188cdff7abd2c6cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:16:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give AI Engine/Trustpilot/Reddit/Twitter Watch real Configure
 panels

Each of these 4 Reputation Manager skills already had a real, verified
server-side action (ad-hoc AI engine check, Outscraper cutoff scan,
Reddit timeframe widen, X since: scan) reachable only through Teammates
chat, with no dashboard UI path to it and no Configure entry point on
either the engagement page or the Library. Pause/resume already worked
for these via the existing Skills panel toggle (engagementSkills.enabled)
- that part wasn't actually missing, contrary to what I told the user.

Adds one Configure form per skill (mirroring the existing worker-config-
forms pattern) that calls the same POST rep-findings/trigger actions chat
already uses, and wires hasHingesPanel: true for all 4 into both places
that render a worker's inline Configure form (the engagement page's
WorkersPanel and the Library's ProductDetailClient) so the Configure
button now actually opens something instead of falling through to a
blank panel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AkznvRLnBokzbdmJ2WwaEM
